---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config/site.config';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description={`Which cookies and local storage ${SITE.name} uses, what each one does, and how to control them in your browser.`}
  lede="What we store on your device, and why."
  lastUpdated={new Date('2026-08-02')}
>
  <div class="not-prose mb-8 rounded-lg border border-[var(--color-warning)]/40 bg-[var(--color-warning)]/10 p-4 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]">
    <strong class="text-[var(--text)]">Template notice:</strong> this policy is a
    good-faith starting point, not legal advice. Confirm it matches what your deployed
    site actually sets before relying on it.
  </div>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>
    This site sets <strong>no advertising cookies and no cross-site tracking cookies</strong>.
    The only thing we store by default is your light/dark theme preference, and that never
    leaves your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>What we store</h2>

  <div class="not-prose my-6 overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full border-collapse text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr class="bg-[var(--bg-alt)]">
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5 text-left font-semibold">Name</th>
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5 text-left font-semibold">Type</th>
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5 text-left font-semibold">Purpose</th>
          <th class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5 text-left font-semibold">Duration</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody class="text-[var(--text-muted)]">
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5"><code>theme</code></td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Local storage</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">
            Remembers whether you chose light or dark mode
          </td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Until you clear it</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5"><code>_cfuvid</code> / <code>__cf_bm</code></td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Cookie (Cloudflare)</td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">
            Bot management and rate limiting by our hosting provider
          </td>
          <td class="border border-[var(--border)] p-2.5">Session / 30 minutes</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>If analytics are enabled</h2>
  <p>
    Where a privacy-preserving analytics provider is enabled, it may set a cookie or use
    local storage to count unique visits in aggregate. These are strictly measurement
    cookies, are never used for advertising, and are never shared with ad networks. Any
    analytics in use is named in the <a href="/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party requests</h2>
  <p>
    Web fonts are requested from Google Fonts. This does not set a cookie, but the request
    necessarily discloses your IP address to that service. Self-hosting the fonts removes
    that request entirely if it matters to you.
  </p>

  <h2>Controlling cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings — every major browser supports
    this under Privacy or Site Settings. Clearing local storage will reset your theme
    preference to follow your operating system. Nothing on this site breaks if you block
    all storage.
  </p>

  <h2>Do Not Track</h2>
  <p>
    We do not perform cross-site tracking, so a DNT or Global Privacy Control signal
    changes nothing about how we treat you.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.organization.email}`}>{SITE.organization.email}</a>.
  </p>
</PageLayout>
